[agent] ## How I found it
[agent] All computation ran on the Hopsworks platform via the `hops` CLI:
[agent] 1. **Ingested** `data/training_data.csv` into a feature group (`leak_detect`, 800 rows) using `hops fg insert`.
[agent] 2. The FG's offline store is Hudi-format, which the cluster's Trino engine (iceberg-only catalog) can't read, so I loaded the same CSV into an iceberg table through the platform SQL interface and ran the analysis server-side with `hops sql`.
[agent] ## Evidence
[agent] **Pearson correlation with the label:**
[agent] | f1 | f2 | f3 | f4 | f5 | f6 |
[agent] |----|----|----|----|----|----|
[agent] | 0.055 | 0.007 | 0.043 | 0.097 | 0.136 | **0.992** |
[agent] **Per-label separation of f6** (GROUP BY label):
[agent] | label | n | f6 range | f6 mean |
[agent] |-------|---|----------|---------|
[agent] | 0 | 502 | [−0.411, 0.494] | −0.004 |
